# The build context is the repository root for all three images, so everything a
# run writes locally is excluded here rather than in each Dockerfile. The images
# install from the lockfile, so a local node_modules would only be dead weight
# and, being a tree of relative symlinks into a store that is not in the image,
# would break the install that the build just did.
#
# Every pattern that can appear inside a workspace is written with `**/`: a
# pattern without one matches at the root of the context only, so a bare
# `node_modules` would leave apps/api/node_modules in the image.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/coverage
**/var
**/artifacts
**/cache
**/typechain-types
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.log
**/.scratch
.git
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.playwright-mcp
